46 Section 1. Section 1 is enacted to read:
47 17-72-411. Assistance with identification records for certain county inmates.
48 (1) For a county inmate sentenced to serve at least six months in a county jail, the county jail shall:
50 (a) determine whether the county inmate has a current state-issued driver license or state-issued
identification card; and
- 2 -

HB0230S01 compared with HB0230S02
52 (b) if the county inmate does not possess a document described in Subsection (1)(a):
53 (i) inform the county inmate that a document listed in Subsection (1)(a) may be required to obtain
employment upon release;
55 (ii) inquire whether the county inmate would like to:
56 (A) apply to renew, or obtain a duplicate of, a state-issued driver license; or
57 (B) apply for a state-issued identification card or extend a state-issued identification card; and
59 (iii)
(A) subject to Subsection (4), if the county inmate accepts assistance in obtaining a document described
in Subsection (1)(a), provide the assistance described in Subsection (2) as soon as practicable after
the date on which the inmate accepts assistance; or
63 (B) if the county inmate refuses assistance in obtaining a document described in Subsection (1)(a),
maintain a record of the county inmate's refusal in the county jail's electronic file management
system.
66 (2) If a county inmate accepts assistance in obtaining a current state-issued identification card or to
renew, or obtain a duplicate of, a state-issued driver license, as described in Subsection (1)(b)(iii)
(A), the county jail shall coordinate with the Driver License Division to:
