95 Section 2. Section 2 is enacted to read:
96 26B-2-136. Drug test result disclosure requirements for substance abuse treatment
programs.
A substance abuse treatment program shall provide the results of a drug test for a
participant in the substance abuse treatment program who is on probation or parole to the
probation or parole officer assigned to supervise the participant if:
102 (1) the participant's supervising probation or parole officer requests the drug test results; and
103 (2) the participant has signed a waiver, in compliance with federal health information disclosure laws,
that allows the substance abuse treatment program to notify the participant's supervising probation
or parole officer regarding the participant's drug test results.
